Temporary XPU test tooling for mkrze/torchrec xpu/train-infer. NOT part of the RFC.

A setup.py option to build against fbgemm-gpu-cpu (TORCHREC_USE_FBGEMM_CPU=1) for XPU
hosts. The XPU tests of the change are in the branch itself
(torchrec/distributed/tests/test_quant_sequence_xpu.py, test_fused_embedding_xpu.py). The
DLRM-v3 XPU test framework applies this patch before its TorchRec rows.

Apply after checking out this branch (working tree only, nothing is committed):

    git apply patches/xpu_test_tooling.patch

Remove it again with `git apply -R patches/xpu_test_tooling.patch`.
Update after changing the branch: apply the patch, adjust the code, then
replace everything below this header with `git diff HEAD -- setup.py torchrec`
(plus new files) and remove the patch from the working tree. Before the RFC,
drop the commit that adds this file.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 7708075f..a9f3b482 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -63,6 +63,16 @@ def main(argv: List[str]) -> None:
         reqs = f.read()
         install_requires = reqs.strip().split("\n")
 
+    # Temporary (XPU test framework): build against fbgemm-gpu-cpu on XPU hosts.
+    fbgemm_cpu = os.environ.get("TORCHREC_USE_FBGEMM_CPU", "0")
+    if fbgemm_cpu not in ("0", "1"):
+        raise ValueError("TORCHREC_USE_FBGEMM_CPU must be 0 or 1")
+    if fbgemm_cpu == "1":
+        install_requires = [
+            "fbgemm-gpu-cpu" if requirement == "fbgemm-gpu" else requirement
+            for requirement in install_requires
+        ]
+
     version, sha = _get_version()
     _export_version(version, sha)
 
